  <h2 class="sec-title">📌 General Questions - About LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</h2>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>1. What is LearnHTMLCSSJS.com? <span>+</span></summary><p><b>LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</b> is a free online learning platform where you can learn <b>HTML, CSS and JavaScript from zero to web developer</b> in simple English. We have 30 lessons, 30 tests, a live playground, dashboard, ranking system and free certificate. Our mission is simple: every student in Pakistan, India, Bangladesh and worldwide should learn coding free, without paying thousands of rupees for expensive courses. You do not need to install any software. You just need a mobile phone and internet. Open <a href="/lesson1">Lesson 1</a> and start learning today.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>2. Is this course really 100% free? Is there any hidden fee? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, <b>100% free forever</b>. All 30 lessons, all tests, playground, dashboard, ranking and certificate are free. We never ask for credit card, bank account, JazzCash or Easypaisa. We never ask for any payment. How do we keep it free? We show a few ads and we believe education should be free. If any website asks you money in our name, it is fake. Our only official website is <b>LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</b>.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>3. Do I need a laptop to learn coding? <span>+</span></summary><p>No. You can learn <b>100% on mobile</b>. Our website is fully mobile responsive. All lessons, tests and playground work on mobile. Many of our students learn only on mobile and build their first website on mobile. If you have a laptop, it is even better, but it is not required. If you can use WhatsApp and Facebook on mobile, you can learn HTML on mobile.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>4. What is the age limit to learn HTML, CSS and JavaScript? <span>+</span></summary><p>There is no age limit. Our course is for students of <b>Class 6 to University</b>, job seekers, teachers, shop owners, housewives, business owners and anyone who wants to learn a new skill. Our youngest students are 11-12 years old and oldest are 45+ years old. If you are under 13, please use the website with your parent or teacher's permission. Coding is for everyone. Age does not matter, practice matters.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>5. Do I need to know English to learn this course? <span>+</span></summary><p>No, you need only basic English. We teach in <b>very simple English</b>, not difficult technical English. Every lesson uses short sentences, simple words and lots of examples. Even if your English is weak, you will understand. HTML, CSS and JavaScript themselves use English words like <code>head</code>, <code>body</code>, <code>color</code>, <code>button</code> - which are very easy to remember. After 10 lessons, your English will also improve.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>6. Do I need to know Maths to learn web development? <span>+</span></summary><p>No. For HTML and CSS, you need zero Maths. For basic JavaScript, you need only plus, minus, multiply, divide - which everyone knows. You do not need to be a Maths genius to become a web developer. Web development is about creativity, design and logic, not difficult Maths. If you can count money in a shop, you can learn JavaScript.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>7. How do I create a free account? <span>+</span></summary><p>Very easy. Click on <a href="/signup">Signup Free</a>, enter your name, username, email and password, and click Signup. Your account will be created in 30 seconds. After signup, you can <a href="/login">Login</a> anytime to see your dashboard, progress, scores and ranking. Your progress is saved automatically. If you forget your password, use the Forgot Password option or contact us.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>8. Can I learn without creating an account? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, you can read <a href="/lesson1">Lesson 1</a> without an account. But to save your progress, give tests, see your scores, compete in ranking and get a certificate, you need a free account. Without an account, your progress will not be saved. We strongly recommend creating a free account - it takes only 30 seconds.</p></details>

  <!-- ============ HTML ============ -->
  <h2 class="sec-title">🧱 HTML Questions - Learn HTML Free</h2>

  <details data-cat="html"><summary>9. What is HTML? <span>+</span></summary><p><b>HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.</b> It is the foundation of every website. Without HTML, there is no website. HTML is used to create structure - headings, paragraphs, images, links, lists, tables, forms, buttons, div, span and semantic tags. When you see a heading on Google, it is made with <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>. When you see a button, it is made with <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>. HTML is the easiest language in the world. You can learn it in 10 days. Start from <a href="/lesson1">Lesson 1 - What is HTML?</a></p></details>

  <details data-cat="html"><summary>10. How long does it take to learn HTML? <span>+</span></summary><p>If you do 1 lesson per day, you will learn HTML in <b>10 days</b> because our course has Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only for HTML. If you do 2 lessons per day, you will learn HTML in 5 days. HTML is very easy. Most students say HTML is easier than English. After HTML, you will learn CSS in next 10 lessons.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="html"><summary>11. What is the difference between HTML and HTML5? <span>+</span></summary><p>HTML5 is the latest version of HTML. It has new tags like <code>&lt;header&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;section&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;article&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;audio&gt;</code>. In our course, we teach <b>HTML5</b> only, because it is modern and used by all websites today. You do not need to learn old HTML. Learn HTML5 directly.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="html"><summary>12. Do I need to memorize all HTML tags? <span>+</span></summary><p>No. You need to learn only 20-25 important tags. In real life, professional developers also do not memorize all tags. They use Google. Our course focuses on important tags: h1 to h6, p, a, img, ul, ol, li, table, form, input, button, div, span, header, footer, section. If you learn these, you can build 90% of websites. We teach you with practice, not memorization.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="html"><summary>13. What is semantic HTML? <span>+</span></summary><p>Semantic HTML means using tags that have meaning. For example, use <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> for header, <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> for navigation, <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code> for footer, <code>&lt;article&gt;</code> for article. This helps Google understand your website and improves SEO. We teach semantic HTML in <a href="/lesson9">Lesson 9</a>. It is very important for jobs and freelancing.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="html"><summary>14. Can I build a full website with only HTML? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, you can build a simple website with only HTML, but it will look plain without CSS. That is why after HTML, you must learn CSS for design and JavaScript for interactivity. In our course, after Lesson 10, you will build an HTML Project, and after Lesson 21, you will build a full website with HTML + CSS.</p></details>

  <!-- ============ CSS ============ -->
  <h2 class="sec-title">🎨 CSS Questions - Learn CSS Free</h2>

  <details data-cat="css"><summary>15. What is CSS? <span>+</span></summary><p><b>CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.</b> CSS is used to design a website. Colors, fonts, spacing, borders, layout, Flexbox, Grid, animations and responsive design - everything is done with CSS. Without CSS, a website looks plain and boring. With CSS, the same website looks modern, beautiful and professional. Start from <a href="/lesson11">Lesson 11 - What is CSS?</a></p></details>

  <details data-cat="css"><summary>16. How long does it take to learn CSS? <span>+</span></summary><p>CSS takes <b>10 days</b> in our course - Lesson 11 to Lesson 20. CSS is a little harder than HTML because it has many properties, but with practice it becomes easy. The secret is: do not just read, practice in our playground. Change colors, try Flexbox, make buttons. After 10 days, you will be able to design beautiful websites.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="css"><summary>17. What is Flexbox and Grid? Which one is better? <span>+</span></summary><p>Flexbox and Grid are two layouts in CSS. <b>Flexbox</b> is best for one row or one column - like navbar, buttons, cards in a line. <b>Grid</b> is best for full page layout - like 2 columns, 3 columns, gallery. Both are important. We teach Flexbox in <a href="/lesson15">Lesson 15</a> and Grid in <a href="/lesson16">Lesson 16</a>. In real jobs, you will use both every day.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="css"><summary>18. What is responsive design? <span>+</span></summary><p>Responsive design means your website looks good on <b>mobile, tablet and laptop</b>. Today, 80% people open websites on mobile. If your website is not mobile-friendly, clients will not like it. We teach responsive design with media queries in <a href="/lesson17">Lesson 17</a>. After that lesson, you will be able to make any website mobile-friendly.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="css"><summary>19. What is the difference between inline, internal and external CSS? <span>+</span></summary><p><b>Inline CSS:</b> Style written inside a tag, like <code>&lt;p style="color:red"&gt;</code>. <b>Internal CSS:</b> Style written in <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> tag inside head. <b>External CSS:</b> Style written in separate .css file and linked. For real projects, external CSS is best because it keeps code clean and fast. We teach all three with examples.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="css"><summary>20. Do I need to learn Tailwind or Bootstrap after CSS? <span>+</span></summary><p>First learn pure CSS properly from our course. After that, you can learn Tailwind CSS or Bootstrap in 2-3 days because they are just shortcuts for CSS. If you skip pure CSS and directly learn Tailwind, you will get confused. Our advice: complete Lesson 11 to 20 first, then learn Tailwind. We will add a Tailwind lesson soon.</p></details>

  <!-- ============ JS ============ -->
  <h2 class="sec-title">🧠 JavaScript Questions - Learn JavaScript Free</h2>

  <details data-cat="js"><summary>21. What is JavaScript? Is it same as Java? <span>+</span></summary><p><b>JavaScript is a programming language</b> that makes a website interactive and smart. When you click a button and something happens, that is JavaScript. When a timer runs, a form shows an error, a menu opens, or a quiz shows your score - all that is JavaScript. <b>Java and JavaScript are totally different.</b> Java is used for Android apps, JavaScript is used for websites. Do not confuse them. Their names are similar but they are different languages.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="js"><summary>22. Is JavaScript difficult to learn? <span>+</span></summary><p>JavaScript is a little harder than HTML and CSS because it is a real programming language. But in our course, we teach JavaScript in very simple way with examples - variables, functions, if-else, loops, events. If you practice daily, you will learn it in 10-15 days. The key is: do not fear JavaScript, just practice small examples daily. Every expert was once a beginner.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="js"><summary>23. What is the difference between HTML, CSS and JavaScript? <span>+</span></summary><p>Think of a human body. <b>HTML = Skeleton (Structure)</b> - bones, headings, paragraphs. <b>CSS = Skin and Clothes (Design)</b> - colors, beauty, style. <b>JavaScript = Brain (Logic)</b> - thinking, movement, interaction. To build a complete website, you need all three. That is why our course teaches all three together in 30 lessons.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="js"><summary>24. After JavaScript, what should I learn next? <span>+</span></summary><p>After completing our 30 lessons, your next steps should be: 1) Learn <b>React.js</b> - most popular JavaScript library for jobs, 2) Learn <b>Node.js + Express</b> for backend, 3) Learn <b>MongoDB</b> for database, 4) Learn <b>Git & GitHub</b>. This combination is called <b>MERN Stack</b> and it has very high demand and high salary in Pakistan and worldwide. We will add React course soon on LearnHTMLCSSJS.com.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="js"><summary>25. Can I get a job with only HTML, CSS and JavaScript? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, you can get <b>internship, junior frontend developer job, and freelancing work</b> with only HTML, CSS and JavaScript. Many companies hire frontend interns who know these three. For high salary jobs, you will need React also, but HTML CSS JS is the foundation. Without this foundation, you cannot learn React. So complete this course first, build 3-4 projects, make a portfolio, then apply for jobs.</p></details>

