  <h2 class="sec-title">🏆 Tests, Scores, Ranking & Certificate</h2>

  <details data-cat="test"><summary>26. How does the test system work? <span>+</span></summary><p>After every lesson, there is a <b>10-question test of 100 marks</b>. Each question is 10 marks. You must score <b>80 or more to pass</b> and unlock the next lesson. Test is only 3 minutes. If you fail, do not worry - read the lesson again and try again. There is no limit on attempts. This system makes sure you really learn, not just skip lessons.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="test"><summary>27. What happens if I fail a test? <span>+</span></summary><p>Nothing bad happens. You can try again unlimited times. Your best score is saved. We recommend reading the lesson again, understanding examples, and then giving the test again. Many students fail first time and pass second time. Failing is part of learning. Do not give up.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="test"><summary>28. Will I get a certificate? Is it free? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, after passing <a href="/lesson30">Lesson 30 Final Exam</a>, you will get a <b>free certificate</b> with your name, course name, and completion date. Certificate is 100% free. You can download it, print it, add it to your CV, LinkedIn, Fiverr and Upwork profiles. It will help you get jobs and clients because it proves you completed a full course.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="test"><summary>29. How does the ranking system work? <span>+</span></summary><p>Ranking is based on your <b>total marks</b> from all tests. The more lessons you complete with high scores, the higher your rank. You can see your rank on <a href="/ranking">Ranking Page</a> and your total marks on <a href="/dashboard">Dashboard</a>. Top students get featured. This creates healthy competition and motivates you to learn more. Cheating in tests is not allowed - fake scores will be removed.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="test"><summary>30. Can I reset my progress and start again? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, email us at <a href="mailto:contact@learnhtmlcssjs.com">contact@learnhtmlcssjs.com</a> with your username and subject "Reset Progress" and we will reset your scores within 24 hours. Or you can create a new account with a different email. Many students reset after 1 month to revise the full course again.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="test"><summary>31. How can I delete my account? <span>+</span></summary><p>Email us at <a href="mailto:contact@learnhtmlcssjs.com">contact@learnhtmlcssjs.com</a> with subject "Delete My Account" and your username. We will delete your account, scores, progress and all data within 7 days, as per our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>. After deletion, your name will also be removed from ranking.</p></details>

  <!-- ============ CAREER ============ -->
  <h2 class="sec-title">💰 Career, Jobs & Freelancing - Earn Money Online</h2>

  <details data-cat="career"><summary>32. Can I really earn money after learning HTML, CSS and JavaScript? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, 100%. After Lesson 25, you will be able to build websites for local shops, schools, and businesses. In Pakistan, a simple business website costs Rs. 10,000 to Rs. 50,000. On Fiverr, a landing page gig starts from $20 to $100. On Upwork, frontend developers earn $10 to $30 per hour. But earning does not come in 1 day. You must practice, build 3-4 projects, make a portfolio, and then start applying. Students who practice daily start earning in 2-3 months.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="career"><summary>33. How to start freelancing on Fiverr and Upwork? <span>+</span></summary><p>We teach complete freelancing guide in <a href="/lesson28">Lesson 28 - Freelancing Guide</a>. Short steps: 1) Complete all 30 lessons, 2) Build 3 projects - portfolio, landing page, business website, 3) Create Fiverr account, 4) Create gigs like "I will make responsive HTML website", 5) Use good title, description and portfolio images, 6) Start with low price, get first 5 orders, get 5-star reviews, then increase price. Consistency is key. Do not give up after 1 week.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="career"><summary>34. How much can a beginner earn from web development in Pakistan? <span>+</span></summary><p>Beginner freelancers in Pakistan earn <b>Rs. 20,000 to Rs. 80,000 per month</b> in first 6 months if they work consistently. After 1 year with React and good portfolio, they earn Rs. 100,000 to Rs. 300,000 per month or more. Job salary for junior frontend developer in Lahore, Karachi, Islamabad is Rs. 40,000 to Rs. 100,000 per month. It depends on your skills, portfolio, communication and consistency. Skills + Practice = Income.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="career"><summary>35. Do I need a degree to become a web developer? <span>+</span></summary><p>No. Web development is a skill-based field. Companies and clients care about your <b>skills and portfolio</b>, not your degree. Many successful developers in Pakistan have no CS degree. They learned from free websites like ours, built projects, and got jobs. Degree helps, but it is not required. If you have skills, you will get work. Focus on building 5 strong projects.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="career"><summary>36. What is SEO? Why is it important? <span>+</span></summary><p><b>SEO stands for Search Engine Optimization.</b> It means making your website appear on Google when someone searches. For example, if someone searches "best biryani in Lahore", Google shows websites with good SEO on top. If your website is on Google first page, you get more customers. We teach SEO basics in <a href="/lesson26">Lesson 26</a> - title, meta description, headings, keywords, alt text, sitemap. Every web developer must know basic SEO.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="career"><summary>37. How to deploy a website free? <span>+</span></summary><p>We teach free deployment in <a href="/lesson27">Lesson 27</a>. You can deploy free on <b>Netlify, Vercel, GitHub Pages, Render</b>. Steps: 1) Make your HTML, CSS, JS files, 2) Create free account on Netlify, 3) Upload your files or connect GitHub, 4) You get a free link like yoursite.netlify.app. You can share this link with clients and in your CV. No money needed for hosting in beginning.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="career"><summary>38. What are interview questions for HTML CSS jobs? <span>+</span></summary><p>We have full list in <a href="/lesson29">Lesson 29 - Interview Questions</a>. Common questions: What is HTML? What is difference between div and span? What is box model? What is Flexbox vs Grid? What is difference between class and id? What is responsive design? What is JavaScript closure? Prepare these 50 questions and you will pass any junior frontend interview. Practice answering in English, not just reading.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="career"><summary>39. Can I learn React after this course? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, React is the next step. React is a JavaScript library used by Facebook, Instagram, Netflix, Airbnb. After completing our 30 lessons, you will be ready for React because React needs strong HTML, CSS and JavaScript. We are planning to add a free React course soon on LearnHTMLCSSJS.com. Till then, complete this course and build projects.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="career"><summary>40. Can I teach others after completing this course? <span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, teaching is the best way to learn. After completing the course, you can teach your friends, siblings, classmates, or even start a YouTube channel. Many students start teaching in their village or school and earn respect and money. Just do not copy our full lessons and sell them. You can teach in your own words and share link to our website.</p></details>

  <!-- ============ MORE ============ -->
  <h2 class="sec-title">❓ More Common Questions</h2>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>41. Is HTML a programming language? <span>+</span></summary><p>No, HTML is a <b>markup language</b>, not a programming language. It is used to structure content. CSS is a styling language. JavaScript is a real programming language. Many beginners ask this in interviews, so remember: HTML = Markup, CSS = Style, JavaScript = Programming.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>42. Which is best - Web Development or App Development? <span>+</span></summary><p>For beginners, <b>Web Development is best</b> because it is easier, needs only browser, no expensive software, and you can start earning faster. App development needs more time and learning Java/Kotlin or Flutter. Start with web development, earn money, then if you want, learn app development later. Web development is the best first skill.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>43. How many hours should I study daily? <span>+</span></summary><p><b>1 hour daily is enough.</b> 30 minutes reading lesson + 30 minutes practice + test. Consistency is more important than long hours. Studying 1 hour daily for 30 days is better than studying 10 hours in 1 day and then stopping. Make a habit: same time daily, no mobile distraction, 1 lesson per day. You will finish in 30 days.</p></details>

  <details data-cat="general"><summary>44. What if I get stuck in a lesson? <span>+</span></summary><p>Do not worry, everyone gets stuck. Steps: 1) Read lesson again slowly, 2) Try example in playground, 3) Search on Google or YouTube, 4) Ask in comments or <a href="/contact">Contact Us</a>. We reply within 24 hours. Also, you can skip and come back next day - sometimes your brain understands better after rest. Never quit because of one difficult lesson.</p></details>

